# Current events in town, part four: gossip ({subject} {claim}: a rumour, which reads as a sentence) and a speaker's
# own news ({news}: what happened to them, in the first person, like "I married Tamsin").

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Gossip

scene et_gos_whisper
when topic=gossip
a : Lean in. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. You didn't hear it from me. | Word at the well is that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Don't spread it, but #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b[old] : I've heard worse about better wolves. And better about worse.
b[priest] : The Bright One frowns on a loose tongue, you know.
b : I never hear anything from you. | The well knows everything. | Who would I tell?
a : Good. | It always does. | Everyone, by supper.

scene et_gos_disbelief
when topic=gossip
a : They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Apparently #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | You'll love this. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : Never. Not #topic.subject#. | Apparently, apparently. Who says? | I don't love it. I don't believe it.
a : That's what I said. | Half the street. | Suit yourself.
b?[friends] : Tell me everything anyway.

scene et_gos_delight
when topic=gossip pair.band=friends
a : Oh, you'll want to sit down. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | I've been saving this one for you. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Guess who #topic.claim#? #topic.subject#!
b : I'm sitting. Go on. | You're a treasure. Go on. | No! Really?
a : That's all I've got. Isn't it enough? | That's it. That's the whole of it. | Really and truly.
b?[adolescent] : I'm telling everyone.

scene et_gos_scold
when topic=gossip pair.band=spouses|family
a : Did you know #topic.subject# #topic.claim#? | The whole street's saying #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Mother says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : And you believe the street? | The street says a lot of things. | Your mother says a lot of things.
a : Sometimes the street's right. | It does. | Don't start.

scene et_gos_merchant
when topic=gossip b.role=merchant
a : I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Word is #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Is it true #topic.subject# #topic.claim#?
b : Then #topic.subject# pays coin first, from now on. | Hm. I'll check my ledger. | If it is, they owe me an explanation.
a : Wise. | Do. | And money, probably.

scene et_gos_guard
when topic=gossip b.role=guard
a : Did you know #topic.subject# #topic.claim#? | They're saying #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | I'd look into #topic.subject#, if I were the watch. They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : I don't arrest wolves for rumours. | Saying's not proof. | If they break a law, I'll look.
a : Shame. | It's a start. | Fair.

scene et_gos_child
when topic=gossip a.stage=young|adolescent
a : I heard the grown-ups say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Everyone says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Is that bad? | #topic.subject# #topic.claim#! I heard it!
b : You shouldn't listen at doors. | Never you mind. | Hush. That's grown-up talk.
a : I wasn't. Much. | But is it? | Everyone knows.

scene et_gos_old
when topic=gossip a.stage=old
a : In my day, if a wolf #topic.claim#, we'd not stop talking for a year. Now it's #topic.subject#. | #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Their grandmother would weep. | Mark me. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I know the signs.
b : We're not stopping now either. | She would. | You always know the signs.
a : Good. | Loudly. | I'm always right.

scene et_gos_petty
when topic=gossip
a : #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. And they had the cheek to sit in the front pew. | #topic.subject# #topic.claim#, and still walks about with that nose in the air. | #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. And wore a new hat to market.
b : The front pew! | That nose. | A new hat! The nerve.
a : The front pew. | Higher than ever. | Feathers on it, too.

scene et_gos_tavern
when topic=gossip here.place=tavern
a : Keep your voice down. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Over the ale, I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Barkeep says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b[innkeeper] : Don't put that on me. I just pour.
b : I'm whispering. | Ale talks. | Barkeeps hear everything.
a : Good. | It does. | Everything.

scene et_gos_defend
when topic=gossip pair.band=friends|acquaintances
a : People say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | They're saying #topic.subject# #topic.claim#, poor thing. | There's talk that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b[family] : That's my kin you're talking about.
b : I don't care what people say. | Poor thing indeed. | There's always talk.
a : Nor should you. | Poor thing. | Always.

scene et_gos_rivals
when topic=gossip pair.band=rivals
a : I suppose you've heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Your friend. | #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Don't pretend you're surprised. | Tell your friend #topic.subject# that everyone knows they #topic.claim#.
b : Not my friend. | I'm not pretending anything. | Tell them yourself.
a : Not any more, I'd think. | Course not. | Maybe I will.

scene et_gos_market
when topic=gossip here.place=market
a : Heard it at the fish stall. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Over the cabbages: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Whole market's saying #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b[merchant] : My stall's a market stall, not a gossip stall. Buying anything?
b : The fish stall's never wrong. | Cabbages and scandal. | Whole market's slow today.
a : Never. | My favourite. | Not the tongues.

scene et_gos_skeptic
when topic=gossip
a : #topic.subject# #topic.claim#, they say. | I keep hearing #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Some say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b[scholar] : I'd want three witnesses before I believed the sun rose.
b : Who's they? | Keep hearing it from whom? | Some say anything.
a : Everyone, it seems. | The usual mouths. | True.

scene et_gos_shocked
when topic=gossip
a : #topic.subject# #topic.claim#! I nearly dropped my basket. | My jaw hit the floor. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | #topic.subject#. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#! Can you imagine?
b : Did you drop it? | Pick it up, then. | I can, actually.
a : Nearly. | Very funny. | You would.

scene et_gos_worry
when topic=gossip pair.band=family|spouses
a : If it's true that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#, what then? | They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Should we stay away? | Folk say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Keep the pups away from them.
b : Then we'll know where we stand. | Let's not be hasty. | I already do.
a : I hope it isn't. | Fine. | Good.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- One's own news

scene et_news_marriage_shy
when topic=news topic.kind=marriage
a : I've something to tell you. #topic.news#. | Don't laugh. #topic.news#. | You'll hear it anyway. #topic.news#.
b[old] : Bless you both. Grow old and rude together.
b : Wonderful! When? | Laugh? I'll cheer! | I'm glad I heard it from you.
a : It's done already. | Cheer quietly. | So am I.
b?[friends] : You didn't invite me! I'll never forgive you. I forgive you.

scene et_news_marriage_tease
when topic=news topic.kind=marriage pair.band=friends
a : Well, it happened. #topic.news#. | #topic.news#. Stop grinning. | I've news. #topic.news#.
b : I knew it! I said so at midsummer! | I'll grin all I like. | About time!
a : You did. Everyone did. | You're insufferable. | It is.

scene et_news_marriage_old
when topic=news topic.kind=marriage a.stage=old
a : At my age! #topic.news#. | Don't look at me like that. #topic.news#. | Love finds the old too. #topic.news#.
b : At any age! Good! | Like what? Like I'm happy for you? | It does!
a : That's the spirit. | Exactly like that. | It did.

scene et_news_loss_raw
when topic=news topic.kind=loss
a : #topic.news#. I don't know what to do with myself. | It's hard to say. #topic.news#. | #topic.news#. The house is so quiet.
b[priest] : The Bright One holds them. And I'll hold you, if you'll let me.
b[old] : Keep busy. Eat. Sleep. Grief walks beside you. It doesn't go.
b : Come and stay with us. | Take your time. | Quiet's the worst of it.
a : I might. | Thank you. | It is.

scene et_news_loss_angry
when topic=news topic.kind=loss pair.band=friends|family
a : #topic.news#. It's not fair. | Why them? #topic.news#. | #topic.news#. I want to break something.
b : No. It isn't. | There's no why. | Break something of mine. I don't mind.
a : None of it is. | Then what's the point? | Don't tempt me.
b?[spouses] : I'm here. I'm not going anywhere.

scene et_news_loss_brave
when topic=news topic.kind=loss a.stage=adult
a : You'll have heard. #topic.news#. I'm managing. | I'm all right. Really. #topic.news#. | #topic.news#. Back at work tomorrow.
b : You don't have to manage. | Are you? | So soon?
a : Someone has to. | No. | Work helps.

scene et_news_loss_child
when topic=news topic.kind=loss a.stage=young|adolescent
a : #topic.news#. Mama won't stop crying. | #topic.news#. Does it mean they're not coming back? | Everyone's sad at home. #topic.news#.
b[old] : Come here, pup. Cry if you want. I'll cry with you.
b : Then you hug her tight. | No, little one. I'm sorry. | That's all right. Sad is all right.
a : I will. | Not ever? | I know.

scene et_news_work_new
when topic=news topic.kind=work
a : Good news for once. #topic.news#. | #topic.news#. Real coin at last. | Guess what? #topic.news#.
b[merchant] : Then you can settle your slate with me, can't you.
b : Well done! | Drinks on you, then. | Tell me!
a : Thank you. | One drink. | I just did.

scene et_news_work_lost
when topic=news topic.kind=work pair.band=friends|family|spouses
a : Bad news, I'm afraid. #topic.news#. | #topic.news#. I'm not sure it's a good thing. | #topic.news#. Everything's changing.
b : What will you do? | Change can be good. | We'll manage.
a : Think. | Can it? | Will we?

scene et_news_work_proud
when topic=news topic.kind=work a.stage=adolescent
a : #topic.news#! I'm earning! | #topic.news#. I'm grown now. | Ma cried when I told her. #topic.news#.
b[old] : Earning's good. Don't spend it all on sweets.
b : Look at you! | Grown? Nearly. | She would.
a : Look at me! | Nearly grown. | Happy tears.

scene et_news_crime_victim
when topic=news topic.kind=crime
a : I have to tell someone. #topic.news#. | #topic.news#. I'm still shaking. | You'll hear it anyway. #topic.news#.
b[guard] : Did you report it? Tell me everything, slowly.
b[healer] : Sit down. Let me look at you.
b : Bright One. Are you hurt? | Sit down. Breathe. | I'm so sorry.
a : Not badly. | I'm trying. | So am I.
b?[friends] : Sleep at ours tonight. I won't hear no.

scene et_news_crime_angry
when topic=news topic.kind=crime pair.band=friends|family|spouses
a : #topic.news#. I'll find who did it. | #topic.news#. In our own home. | #topic.news#. And the watch shrugged.
b : Let the watch do it. | That's the worst of it. Home. | Then we'll shout until they don't.
a : They won't. | Nowhere's safe. | Loudly.

scene et_news_crime_acq
when topic=news topic.kind=crime pair.band=strangers|acquaintances
a : Bad week. #topic.news#. | #topic.news#. Thought you should know, living near. | #topic.news#. Lock your doors.
b : I'm sorry to hear it. | Thank you for telling me. | I will.
a : Thank you. | Neighbours ought to. | Do.

scene et_news_generic
when topic=news
weight 0.5
a : #topic.news#. That's my news. | Did you hear? #topic.news#. | #topic.news#. Thought you'd want to know.
b : That's quite something. | I hadn't heard. | Thank you for telling me.
a : It is. | Now you have. | Of course.
